  "id": "COMPOUND:27259 - PROTEIN:6320",
  "verbalization": "Sophoraflavanone A is shown to interact with multiple targets, including the phosphorylase b kinase gamma catalytic chain, the B1 bradykinin receptor, and ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1. These targets are all involved in signaling and cellular processes, and their interaction with Sophoraflavanone A suggests a potential role in modulating these pathways. The evidence points to a shared mechanism where Sophoraflavanone A may influence cellular functions through the activation or inhibition of these targets, which in turn could affect the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6. The presence of a common downstream target, (1R,4S,5R,7S,11R,13S,17S,18S,19R)-4,5,17-trihydroxy-14,18-dimethyl-6-methylidene-3,10-dioxapentacyclo[9.8.0.01,7.04,19.013,18]nonadec-14-ene-9,16-dione, indicates a possible regulatory relationship between these targets and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6. This suggests that Sophoraflavanone A may act as a modulator of cellular processes through a network of targets that ultimately influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6.",
